# .saveinclude — the allowlist of paths any brain command may commit.
# One path or glob per line; blank lines and # comments are ignored.
#
# THIS FILE IS THE VAULT'S PERMISSION MODEL. Every command that commits goes
# through bin/vault-commit.sh, and that script does two things with this list:
#   1. it stages only what's listed here — never `git add -A`; and
#   2. it then VERIFIES the whole git index against this list, and refuses the
#      commit if anything outside it is staged.
# (2) is what makes the rule hold: the git index is shared by every session in
# the checkout, so a concurrent session or a stray `git add` can stage anything
# at all. Checking the index — not just being careful about what we add — is what
# turns "we only commit allowlisted paths" from an intention into a property.
#
# A vault with no .saveinclude cannot commit through the tooling at all. That is
# deliberate: there is no safe default. Committing everything would publish
# private content; committing nothing would make every save a silent no-op.
#
# Customize it to your trust model:
#   • ADD a path to let /brain:save commit it directly.
#   • REMOVE (or never list) a path to keep it local / require manual staging.
#   • Want something kept out entirely? Put it under a gitignored path (e.g. chats/)
#     or any folder not listed here — /brain:save will leave it in the working tree.
#
# Deliberately NOT here:
#   • chats/              — harvested transcripts are private (also gitignored).
#   • trusted wiki/ notes — knowledge changes go via PR, staged separately, not /brain:save.

logs/
wiki/hot.md
wiki/log.md

# The vault's OWN concept graph, built over wiki/ (step 5c).
graphify-out/graph.json
graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md
graphify-out/.community-labels.json
graphify-out/manifest.json
graphify-out/brain-inputs.json
graphify-out/communities/

# The mirrored code graphs, one folder per covered repo, written by
# bin/sync-graph.sh. Its commit goes through vault-commit.sh like everything
# else, so leaving this off means the sync copies files and then refuses to
# commit them.
graphify/
